{
  "protocol": "wikantik-collab",
  "protocolVersion": 1,
  "source": "docs/MultiEdit.MD sections 0 (A6, A8, A10-A13), 6.1, 6.2 and the Phase 1 plan amendments (Session core, Task 3)",
  "notes": {
    "basePath": "All paths are under /api/collab/{pageName}. Sample page: PageName.",
    "changes": "Every `changes` value is CodeMirror ChangeSet.toJSON(): a number is an unchanged span, [deleted, ...insertedLines] a replacement. Lengths are UTF-16 code units. Sample doc 'Hello world' is 11 units.",
    "reasonOnEvery409": "Every 409 body carries a `reason` (stale-base, rejoin, frozen, rate-limited, publish-merged-retry, derived-page). The rejoin 409 also keeps the legacy `rejoin:true`, the stale-base 409 keeps `accepted:false` plus the head `version`.",
    "rateLimited": "AMBIGUITY: the controller ruling lists rate-limited as a 409 on POST /updates; the Phase 1 plan amendment (Session core, Task 3, A8) says 429. This fixture records 409 per the ruling. The frontend treats `reason:'rate-limited'` on ANY status (409 or 429) as back off and retry, so either server choice works for the client. Java Task 7 must pick one and the controller must reconcile.",
    "noPresenceEndpoint": "There is no /presence endpoint (A8). The selection {anchor, head, version, unconfirmed} rides on POST /updates (key `selection`, optional; a push with empty `updates` is a presence-only push). anchor/head are in the sender's LOCAL document coordinates; `version` is the sender's synced version and `unconfirmed` the count of its unconfirmed updates (A12), so a receiver maps them through the corresponding updates.",
    "presence": "AMBIGUITY (6.2 says presence:{...}): chosen as a map keyed by participantId of {displayName, color, anchor, head, version, unconfirmed}, excluding the requester, always the full map of other participants when `presenceSeq` > the request's presenceSince, else {}. The response carries `presenceSeq`.",
    "cursors": "AMBIGUITY: 6.2 gives GET /updates a presenceSince cursor but no cursor for `events` or a head version. Chosen: response also carries `metaSeq`, `presenceSeq` and `eventSeq`; every event carries a monotonically increasing `seq`; the request adds `eventsSince`. The new head version is `since + updates.length`.",
    "longPoll": "GET /updates parks up to poll.timeoutSeconds. On timeout it answers 200 with empty updates/metaOps/events and presence {}.",
    "join": "join takes priorClientId (the server reissues it when it still knows it, 7.2), initialText and initialMeta (A11; used only when the join creates the session). `doc` is the document at `version`.",
    "ownUpdates": "A pull returns the caller's own updates too; receiveUpdates recognises them by clientID as confirmations. A 200 on POST /updates does NOT remove them; only the pull does.",
    "publish422": "The 422 bodies are those of PageResource.doPut: {error:'frontmatter_validation_failed'|'access_rule_shape'|'math_validation_failed', violations:[...]}. One example is recorded (frontmatter).",
    "errorBodiesWithoutReason": "400 and 413 use reason 'bad-request' and 'oversize'. 401/403 bodies are the usual RestServletBase error envelope {error, message}."
  },
  "cases": [
